It sort of depends, &nbsp;often I&#39;ll go for long stretches without touching a particular hero and then go crazy with that same hero as I try to figure out either 1. &nbsp;Why I didnt like them in the first place or 2. &nbsp;New strategies that maybe I&#39;ll like them better. &nbsp; &nbsp;Recently I was on a bit of a Nightmist-binge after practically not touching her since IR came out. &nbsp; I&#39;ve done the same thing for Absolute Zero and Mr. Fixer.

&nbsp;

I play relatively few games as Expatriette. &nbsp; Ammo cards are frusterating and she never seems to have what she needs. &nbsp;Then as soon as she gets it, its Devestating Aroura and you&#39;re back to square 1. &nbsp; Fixer is more or less in the same spot though I play him just slightly more I think.

&nbsp;

Argent Adept is at the bottom of the pile for me though. &nbsp;I&#39;d rather play a hero that I feel is weak and fun like Mr. Fixer than one I find strong and a headache, &nbsp;which is where AA fits in. &nbsp; He&#39;s a good hero for sure, &nbsp;but I really dont care to have to search through my deck AGAIN and grumble to myself &nbsp;&quot;freaking.... &nbsp;melody/rhythm... which freaking instrument are you?&quot;. &nbsp; &nbsp;I&#39;m also not &nbsp;a fan of &quot;Arcane Cadence! &nbsp; .... &nbsp;reveal 5, one in my hand, one on top of my deck, one on bottom of my deck, one in the trash and play... Arcane Cadence!.... &nbsp; &nbsp;reveal 5, one in my hand, one on top of my deck....&quot; &nbsp;&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Although, &nbsp; even lower on the totem pole, &nbsp;lower still that I actually forgot about him being a hero, &nbsp;so low that he&#39;s not even in the box... &nbsp; is the Scholar. &nbsp; For much the same reasons I guess. &nbsp; He just has to jump through way too many hoops. &nbsp;And even more than that... &nbsp; He has a cool factor of 0 to me. &nbsp;I can&#39;t get into him. &nbsp; He doesn&#39;t seem like a superhero. &nbsp; He seems like if you took the Justice Leauge and decided you needed a new member and so you were going to add The Dude. &nbsp; &nbsp; Don&#39;t get me wrong, &nbsp;I love The Dude, &nbsp;but I don&#39;t want him fighting crime alongside Batman and Flash. &nbsp; He kills the [i]entire[/i] theme of the game for me.
